## Verified live requests (in-container)

```bash
# Verify current container IP first
hostname -I

# Proxy (current IP)
curl -s http://172.20.33.184:11435/api/tags
curl -s http://localhost:11435/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"model":"gemma3:4b","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"OK"}],"stream":false}'
# → 200 OK, body contains "OK."

# Direct Ollama (container-local only)
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags
```

## Zo provider settings

Path: [Settings → AI → Providers](/?t=settings&s=ai&d=providers)

- Base URL: `http://localhost:11435/v1`
- API key: `ollama`
- Model: `gemma3:1b`
- streaming: disabled (provider UI does not expose a streaming toggle; proxy on 11435 enforces `stream: false`)

## Common failure modes

- Using an old/container-local hostname in Base URL (e.g., `172.20.17.188` or `localhost` when the proxy is bound to the container interface) results in connection failures/timeouts. **Always verify current container IP with `hostname -I`** and point Zo provider to that IP on port 11435.
- “model stream interrupted” = Zo tried streaming. The proxy on 11435 strips/forces non-streaming (`stream: false` in code; deletes `tools`/`functions`). If you still see “stream interrupted”, confirm Zo Base URL hits the proxy (`...:11435/v1`), not direct Ollama (`...:11434`).
- Durable localhost:11435 — no rebuild updates needed.

